course: dictionary
lesson: 6052
title: Working in your mind
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word mentally comes from mind. It tells you where something happens: in your head, in your thoughts, not on paper and not with your hands. «Work it out mentally» means do the sum in your head, with no pencil.
explain: Mentally can also describe how healthy your mind is. «Mentally healthy» means your mind is well, and «mentally tired» means your brain feels worn out, even if your legs are fine. Ask yourself: is this about the mind, the body, or paper?
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «She calculated the answer mentally» still makes sense if you think of it as "in her head". In sport, «mentally prepared» means ready in your mind for the match.
fact: Mentally is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done or where it happens.
fact: «Mentally» means in your mind or thoughts, not on paper or with your body.
fact: «Calculate mentally» means work out a sum in your head; this is called mental maths.
fact: «Mentally» can also mean about the health of the mind: «mentally healthy», «mentally strong», «mentally exhausted».
fact: «Lost his marbles» means became mentally confused or went mad; it is humorous and can be unkind.
exercise: «Work it out mentally, without a pencil.» Where is the working done? | On the board | With your hands | On paper | *In your mind
exercise: «She was mentally prepared for the race.» What does mentally prepared mean? | Lying down with her eyes shut | Ready with a new pair of shoes | *Ready in her mind | Late for the start
exercise: Which of these is mental maths? | *Calculating the answer in your head | Adding up on a calculator | Drawing a bar chart | Measuring a line with a ruler
test: «He was mentally exhausted after the long exam.» What does mentally exhausted mean? | Hungry for lunch | Asleep in bed | *Very tired in the mind | Very tired from running
test: «He has lost his marbles» is an idiom. What does it mean? | Won a game of marbles | Lost his toys in the park | *Became mentally confused or went mad | Felt very happy and proud
exam: Which sentence uses mentally to mean about the health of the mind? | «The runner ran fast.» | «The sum was written on the board.» | *«She is mentally strong after her illness.» | «He drew a map on paper.»
